Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["\<\
Quadratic Gravity: field equations and perturbed FLRW equations\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"7e7e63bd-f502-45e2-8adc-82aebc08bc4a"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook consolidates the two original derivations.  It starts from the \
Stelle quadratic-gravity Lagrangian, builds the metric Euler-Lagrange tensor \
term by term, and then uses xPand to obtain its background and linear scalar \
perturbations about a spatially-flat FLRW spacetime in longitudinal (Newton) \
gauge.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"56912568-b24f-462c-bf57-e8d54ca55a7c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Conventions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f99eec9f-300c-45f6-bd94-7744ffb0000f"],

Cell["\<\
The supplied xPand notebooks use the FLFlat slicing, so the perturbative \
calculation below is for K = 0 and conformal time \[Eta].  The metric used by \
xPand is ds^2 = a(\[Eta])^2[-(1+2 \[CapitalPhi]) d\[Eta]^2 + (1-2 \
\[CapitalPsi]) \[Delta]ij dxi dxj].  Thus, the scale-factor prefactor is kept \
explicitly in the perturbative output.  This is the convention needed for \
compatibility with the two source notebooks.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e0258858-a4d2-4ac9-af18-10506e78b206"],

