Cell["\<\
The displayed result is
G_{mu nu} + 2 alpha R R_{mu nu} - (alpha/2) R^2 g_{mu nu} + 2 alpha Box[R] \
g_{mu nu} - 2 alpha Nabla_mu Nabla_nu R + beta E^(C2)_{mu nu} = T_{mu nu},
where E^(C2)_{mu nu} is the explicit Weyl-squared tensor constructed in the \
preceding cell.  This is the manuscript equation, with qgAlpha = alpha and \
qgBeta = beta.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ec893991-c58f-4858-aabc-3cb9c0c2adea"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Perturbed FLRW setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"fe58d5ae-7842-4a82-93a6-bfb45487e79b"],

Cell["\<\
The calculation follows the FLFlat/NewtonGauge conventions of the supplied \
xPand notebooks.  The spatial curvature is therefore K = 0 and the displayed \
components are the normal-normal (nn), normal-spatial (nh), and \
spatial-spatial (hh) projections.  These are the readable 3+1 counterparts of \
the 00, 0i, and ij coordinate equations.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ff5831b0-701b-4d53-b251-0e9667831669"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
     "xAct", " ", "emits", " ", "many", " ", "registration", " ", "messages", 
      " ", "while", " ", "defining", " ", "the", " ", "3"}], "+", 
